# Polestar Experimental, Riverglades for the Horde, part 4 of 4 (2026-11-12). Hand-written from players'
# recordings of the zone and Forever's quest data for titles, levels, objectives and places.
# Order: the hearth to Rog'mar; Clubtoe's quests in Sunnyglade on the way west; Da'grosh's camp below Twilight's
# Shroud, Crag'rog's cave, the Twilight cult's camps and ogre mine (levels 41-44); out through Twilight's Shroud to
# Kargath (its flight path), where our Feralas & Tanaris guide picks up: the Riverglades take the place of our
# Stranglethorn Vale & Swamp of Sorrows guide for the players who choose them at the end of the Badlands.
# Offered only after another quest is handed in (players' recordings): The Wayward Warrior after Clugfist's Decree;
# The Purple Ones and Sickening Lights after Digging for Answers; the second Purple Ones after the first; Twilight No
# More! after the second Purple Ones; Rise Up! and Death to the Executioner after Rumblings of Discontent; It Is
# Time, Brother... and Bring Me His Head after Carving a Path.
# Elites, each behind a group choice: Chogg'Zac (41), Overlord Kilgar (46). The Twilight camps hold elites the route
# never asks for: Twilight Enforcers (45) on patrol, Executioner Morg and Overlord Kilgar (46) in the fortress, the
# Twilight Forgemaster (46, rare).
# Left out on purpose:
# - Spread the Word (95418) and Land of Giants (95420) after Chogg'Zac: back across the zone to Rog'mar and
#   Bolder'ok.
# - Death to the Executioner (95433): Executioner Morg is an elite (46), and the mace goes to Clugfist in Bolder'ok.
# - It Is Time, Brother... (95278): Da'grosh's message goes back to Krom'rosh in Rog'mar, and this route leaves the
#   zone through Twilight's Shroud instead (a Krol'dok Stronghold runner takes it: below).
# - Key Ingredients (94974): Kreza Darkthorn wants crafted materials.
# Krol'dok Stronghold (`when dungeon "Krol'dok Stronghold"`, dungeons in the route), for a group of five: a character
# who runs it takes Tran'gul's Tome of Twilight (94972) and Krom'rosh's Eye of Mugg (94968) on the Rog'mar stop at the
# start and Da'grosh's A Token of Vengeance (94975) at his camp; the run comes after Bring Me His Head, at 43 (the
# dungeon's floor; players' recordings put the Horde part 4's end at a median of 43), from the door north of
# Sunnyglade, about 256 yd from Da'grosh's camp, where 16 people went in. Da'grosh takes the ears and gives It Is
# Time, Brother... for Krom'rosh; the hearth back to Rog'mar brings the other hand-ins (Tunk the blacksmith's Krol'dok
# Moulding, 94973, for Kreza Darkthorn), and the route goes on from there to Twilight's Shroud.

step Hearth to Rog'mar
  hearth "Rog'mar"

step Rog'mar
  tip Experimental route (alpha): if a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip Krom'rosh in the middle of the fort: Clugfist's word sends him looking for Da'grosh, his warrior in the west.
  turnin 95428                          -- Krom'rosh: Clugfist's Decree
  accept 94744                          -- The Wayward Warrior: for Da'grosh, west of Sunnyglade

step Tran'gul and Krom'rosh
  when dungeon "Krol'dok Stronghold"
  when level>=42.5
  tip For your Krol'dok Stronghold run, at the end of this guide: Tran'gul and Krom'rosh stand side by side in the fort.
  accept 94972                          -- Tran'gul: the Tome of Twilight, from Nar'gurk inside
  accept 94968                          -- Krom'rosh: the Eye of Mugg, from Overlord Mugg inside

step Neza Bloodsnout
  when onquest 95882
  turnin 95882

step Clubtoe
  tip West to Sunnyglade again: Clubtoe, a Twilight miner who wants out, waits at the town's eastern edge. Talk him round, then hand Tran'gul's quest in; one of the missing ogres stands a few steps west.
  complete 94727 @49.9,46.9             -- talk Clubtoe round
  turnin 94727
  accept 95417                          -- The Purple Ones
  accept 95602                          -- Sickening Lights
  turnin 95417                          -- Twilight Brute, a few steps west
  accept 95601                          -- The Purple Ones

step The ritual grounds
  tip The ritualists and their empowered brutes gather at the ritual circles in the middle of Sunnyglade: wreck five of the circles.
  kill 261711 x5 quest 95601.1          -- Empowered Brute
  kill 262169 x10 quest 95601.2         -- Twilight Ritualist
  complete 95602 @47.7,49.9             -- destroy 5 Twilight Ritual Circles

step Clubtoe
  turnin 95601
  turnin 95602

step Chogg'Zac
  when group 95427
  tip Chogg'Zac, the two-headed ogre, is an elite (level 41) at the western edge of Sunnyglade: grouping up is advised.
  accept 95427                          -- Clubtoe: Twilight No More!
  collect 265750 quest 95427.2 @44.9,51.0  -- Chogg's Head
  collect 265751 quest 95427.1 @44.9,51.0  -- Zac's Head
  turnin 95427                          -- Clubtoe

step Da'grosh
  tip West out of Sunnyglade and on up the valley towards Twilight's Shroud: Da'grosh, Krom'rosh's wayward warrior, keeps a camp in the hills below the Twilight cult's fortress.
  turnin 94744                          -- Da'grosh
  accept 95431                          -- Rumblings of Discontent
  accept 94745                          -- Carving a Path
  accept 94748                          -- Break Their Chains

step Da'grosh
  when dungeon "Krol'dok Stronghold"
  when level>=42.8
  accept 94975                          -- Da'grosh: A Token of Vengeance, the cultists' ears inside the stronghold

step Crag'rog
  tip Crag'rog, a Bolder'ok ogre, hides in the cave west of Da'grosh's camp.
  turnin 95431                          -- Crag'rog
  accept 95432                          -- Rise Up!

step The Twilight camps
  tip The cult's camps fill the valley south and west of Da'grosh. Free the captive Rog'mar Scouts as you find them. Twilight Enforcers (elites, level 45) patrol through the camps: watch where they walk before each pull. Overlord Kilgar and Executioner Morg (elites, 46) hold the fortress at the valley's head: pull the cultists away from them. Sergeant Riftan's Alliance camp sits at the valley's south end, and its Farholde Lookouts (level 46) attack the Horde: stay north of it.
  kill 256795 x8 quest 94745.1          -- Twilight Fanatic
  kill 256797 x8 quest 94745.2          -- Twilight Corrupter
  kill 256799 x8 quest 94745.3          -- Twilight Champion
  complete 94748 @29.4,40.5             -- free five captive Rog'mar Scouts

step The ogre mine
  tip North of the camps the cult works ogre miners in a mine: talk five of them into rising up against their masters.
  complete 95432 @26.9,34.9             -- recruit five Ogre Miners

step Crag'rog
  turnin 95432

step Da'grosh
  turnin 94745
  turnin 94748

step Bring Me His Head
  when group 94768
  tip Overlord Kilgar is an elite (level 46) in the fortress at the head of the valley, with the Enforcers around him: grouping up is advised.
  accept 94768                          -- Da'grosh
  collect 265837 quest 94768.1 @26.1,43.9  -- Kilgar's Head
  turnin 94768

step Krol'dok Stronghold
  when dungeon "Krol'dok Stronghold"
  when onquest 94972,94968,94975
  when level>=43
  tip Krol'dok Stronghold is a dungeon for a group of five, levels 40 to 47. Its door is north of Sunnyglade at the foot of the Twilight valley, a short walk from Da'grosh's camp.
  tip Inside: the cultists' ears for Da'grosh (Commander Zarmok's too), the Tome of Twilight from Nar'gurk for Tran'gul and the Eye of Mugg from Overlord Mugg for Krom'rosh. Tunk the blacksmith drops the Krol'dok Moulding, which starts a quest for Kreza Darkthorn in Rog'mar.
  enter "Krol'dok Stronghold" @37.2,43.9
  complete 94975 @37.2,43.9             -- A Token of Vengeance: fifteen Cultist Ears, inside
  complete 94972 @37.2,43.9             -- Tome of Twilight: Nar'gurk, inside
  complete 94968 @37.2,43.9             -- Eye of Mugg: Overlord Mugg, inside

step Da'grosh
  when dungeon "Krol'dok Stronghold"
  when complete 94975
  tip Back to Da'grosh's camp, a short walk from the door.
  turnin 94975                          -- Da'grosh
  accept 95278                          -- Da'grosh: It Is Time, Brother..., for Krom'rosh in Rog'mar

step Hearth to Rog'mar
  when dungeon "Krol'dok Stronghold"
  when onquest 94972,94968,95278,94973
  when level>=43
  hearth "Rog'mar"

step Tran'gul
  when dungeon "Krol'dok Stronghold"
  when complete 94972
  turnin 94972                          -- Tran'gul

step Krom'rosh
  when dungeon "Krol'dok Stronghold"
  when complete 94968
  turnin 94968                          -- Krom'rosh

step Krom'rosh
  when dungeon "Krol'dok Stronghold"
  when onquest 95278
  turnin 95278                          -- Krom'rosh

step Kreza Darkthorn
  when dungeon "Krol'dok Stronghold"
  when onquest 94973
  turnin 94973                          -- Kreza Darkthorn

step Twilight's Shroud
  tip The next guide flies from Kargath in the Badlands: north out of Da'grosh's valley and up through Twilight's Shroud, the way through to the Badlands.
  goto 32.0,29.9 "Twilight's Shroud"

step Kargath
  tip Across the Badlands to Kargath, the Horde fortress built into the cliffs at the zone's western edge: its flight master stands at the foot of the fortress.
  enter "Badlands"
  zone Badlands
  getfp "Kargath"
